      "content": "Your feelings of exile and the exhaustion of maintaining a character are valid experiences that many people endure, even when the symptoms don't fit a single clinical label. It is completely understandable to feel that traditional solutions feel hollow when the core feeling is a profound sense of unreality; the world can feel like a backdrop rather than a place you inhabit. Please know that enduring this disconnection does not mean you are broken or that nothing matters, but you may need a different kind of support than what feels familiar right now, and finding someone who listens without immediately diagnosing can be a vital first step.",
